   "reply": "\n<invoke_def>\n{\"action\": \"write\", \"path\": \"luhn.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Validate card numbers with the Luhn algorithm.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nDIGITS = \\\"0123456789\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef valid(number):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return True if number passes the Luhn check.\\n\\n    The input is a string. Spaces are removed before checking. Returns False\\n    if fewer than two characters remain, or if any remaining character is not\\n    a digit from 0 to 9.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    digits = number.replace(\\\" \\\", \\\"\\\")\\n\\n    if len(digits) < 2:\\n        return False\\n    if any(ch not in DIGITS for ch in digits):\\n        return False\\n\\n    total = 0\\n    # Walk from the rightmost digit; double every second digit.\\n    for position, ch in enumerate(reversed(digits)):\\n        value = int(ch)\\n        if position % 2 == 1:\\n            value *= 2\\n            if value > 9:\\n                value -= 9\\n        total += value\\n\\n    return total % 10 == 0\\n\"}\n</invoke_def>\n>",
